1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:09,460
When you watch TV, brighten the
room and sit back a little, okay?

2
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:22,920
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:30,040
kick a pebble and even your shoe flies off.

4
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:38,480
Will you take me in, I wonder?

5
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:44,520
They laughed at me for still being a kid.

6
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:49,620
Even if I somehow rouse my spirit,

7
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:54,680
Katsushika, Kameari,
not even a yawn changes.

8
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,620
The streetscape feels strangely kind.

9
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:06,460
From the pointed-hat water intake tower,

10
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:12,860
the sunset falls into the great sky.

11
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,320
Tomorrow, too, it ends like this

12
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:25,100
We have no choice but to win,
and happiness comes again, they say.

13
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,820
I only realized it after losing it.

14
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:29,960
Because I'm such a fool.

15
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:39,540
Ryotsu's Ambition: Time Slip Sengoku Den

16
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,560
Basking in the gentle spring sunshine,
how is everyone doing?

17
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:49,680
Speaking of which, the weather
has become so pleasant, hasn't it?

18
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:50,040
Yes, it has.

19
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:53,300
Well, my son also started
first grade this year, so

20
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,380
Let's eat.

21
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:56,500
Let's eat.

22
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,400
Let's leave the seasonal greetings there.

23
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,060
What's today's topic?

24
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:08,140
In a village in the Tohoku region,
a big commotion is happening right now.

25
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,300
Ryo-chan,
you just got your paycheck, though.

26
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,900
What a troublesome-looking lunch.

27
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,020
Ma'am, it's Kame-jirushi.

28
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:16,080
Reiko-san

29
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,340
What's wrong with you?

30
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,060
I bet you got some freebies at the pachinko parlor,
didn't you?

31
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:22,200
Reiko-san

32
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,300
So what?

33
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:25,860
I get it.

34
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,180
Bingo, isn't it, Ryo-chan?

35
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,420
That's why you panicked
in front of Kei-chan.

36
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,700
Reiko-san

37
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,060
What is it now?

38
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:36,340
It's your own fault,
so there's nothing to be done about it.

39
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,660
Reiko, you two...

40
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:40,900
How dare you talk to me like that!

41
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,120
This is Mr. Gonbei Yamada,
who dug up a koban worth 100 million yen.

42
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:54,980
Mr. Yamada, how on earth did you find it?

43
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:59,940
Well, you see, my dog Pochi was
barking up a storm in the field out back.

44
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,980
It was so noisy I got
curious and started digging.

45
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:07,000
And out came oban and koban,
clink, clink, clink!

46
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:11,100
Honestly, I was so shocked
I thought I'd fall right over.

47
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,540
What?!

48
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,820
Meanwhile, my salary's being drained away!

49
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:17,980
Don't mess with me!

50
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:23,240
You wouldn't go and hand it over to TV or anything,
would you?

51
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,260
It's just not fair that
something like this can happen!

52
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,600
As a human being, I can't forgive that.

53
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,860
Some people in this world are just lucky,
I guess.

54
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:30,360
Why don't you dig somewhere too, Ryo-chan?

55
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:33,740
You might find hidden treasure
from the Tokugawa or Toyotomi clans.

56
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:34,900
They did that on TV once, didn't they?

57
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:37,040
Checking old documents
and using metal detectors,

58
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,980
they stretched it out for two whole hours,

59
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:40,300
and nothing ever turned up.

60
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:41,380
Senpai.

61
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:46,920
After all,

62
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,640
Ryo-chan, I'm joking.

63
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:51,500
There's no way there's hidden treasure in a place like this,
you know.

64
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,660
That's right, senpai.

65
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:53,780
You'd better stop.

66
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:55,320
It'll be nothing but a waste of effort.

67
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,920
Even on TV, they stretch it out for
two whole hours and still find nothing.

68
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,340
You can't know until you actually dig,
can you?

69
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,220
Ryo, I've brought a customer!

70
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:04,800
A customer?

71
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,820
I'm busy right now.

72
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:07,980
Please come back later.

73
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:09,760
Ryo-san!

74
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,480
Good thing I dared to.

75
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,280
What's this?

76
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,700
Is she from some ninja
research club or something?

77
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:19,600
Senpai, your connections are really wide-ranging,
aren't they?

78
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,600
She might be a real ninja, you know.

79
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,480
I don't know you, you hear?

80
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:23,920
How cruel!

81
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:27,340
Saying such cold things to a girl
who came all this way to see you!

82
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,080
No, I really don't recognize her.

83
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:30,180
How heartless.

84
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:33,660
Once girls that age get fixated on something,
there's no telling what they'll do.

85
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,440
Don't say scary things!
I really don't know her!

86
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:39,540
Grandpa Rika told me all about you, Ryo-san.

87
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:44,400
Grandpa Rika? Who's that?

88
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:48,700
Grandpa has white hair and a beard,

89
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:51,600
and always wears a purple chanchanko jacket,

90
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:54,660
and swings his cane around, super hyped up.

91
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:56,700
The hyper old man?

92
00:04:57,180 --> 00:05:00,200
You mean that Divine Punishment
old geezer Kayama from Heaven?

93
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:04,340
Ding ding! Bingo!
That's the Divine Punishment old geezer!

94
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:07,160
So that means you're...

95
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,600
That Divine Punishment
old man's granddaughter?

96
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:13,720
My name is Kōme. Nice to meet you.

97
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,380
Weren't you friends with
that cosplay maniac Ryotsu?

98
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:20,620
We can't just stand here chatting,
so why don't you come inside?

99
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:21,720
Okay.

100
00:05:22,740 --> 00:05:25,960
I had no idea Mr. Kayama
had such a cute granddaughter.

101
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:28,600
So what did you come here
to see me for, anyway?

102
00:05:28,860 --> 00:05:30,840
Actually, I ran away from home.

103
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,580
Ran away from home!?

104
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,820
You came all the way from
Heaven to the outside world?

105
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:35,240
Mm-hm.

106
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:39,620
Wouldn't Heaven be way better than the outside world?
Everything's good there, right?

107
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,800
Grandpa's discipline is super strict, so

108
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:44,860
Sado

109
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:48,080
You need to put more snap into it,
don't you?

110
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:48,680
Yes.

111
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,980
Look at this, watch me, like this.

112
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:53,060
Corner

113
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:53,400
Ee.

114
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:57,320
Tell me exactly what you did.

115
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:58,700
Properly, that's right.

116
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:00,200
Chief,

117
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,480
Donki-sized, you

118
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:14,100
You lack spirit,
you lack spirit, Miss Ronjaa.

119
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:18,680
All you ever say is
"study, study," and it's suffocating.

120
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:20,020
Study.

121
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,480
It's Divine Punishment Grandpa.

122
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:26,180
Is there an exam war in heaven too?

123
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:28,360
So every world is the same

124
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,640
I want to have fun sometimes, too.

125
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,420
Down in the mortal world
there's a place called Harajuku,

126
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:37,040
and I hear kids around my age,
about sixteen, hang out there.

127
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,640
So,

128
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:40,500
I understand. I've been through it too.

129
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,640
But of all people,
she came to Ryotsu for help.

130
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:47,251
Because Grandpa is always
talking about Ryo-san,

131
00:06:47,301 --> 00:06:49,220
I've kind of come to feel close to you too.

132
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:52,433
Whenever we were down in the human world,
we always said,

133
00:06:52,483 --> 00:06:54,920
"Let's visit Ryo-san at the Kameari
Park police box in Katsushika Ward."

134
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:57,720
This is just like a Tora-san movie.

135
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:00,796
Yes, I see, I see. That old man
has been talking about me, has he?

136
00:07:00,846 --> 00:07:03,640
Well, I did look after
him in all sorts of ways.

137
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,660
I wonder what he said about me?

138
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:08,088
Let me see, I think he said I have no plan,

139
00:07:08,138 --> 00:07:10,122
that I lead a dissolute life,

140
00:07:10,172 --> 00:07:13,180
and that I'm a hopeless,
good-for-nothing man.

141
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:20,720
That damn old geezer,
so that's why he was saying that, damn it!

142
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:25,678
Wait. If she's that old
man's granddaughter, then...

143
00:07:25,728 --> 00:07:28,760
Can Kōme-chan use magic too?

144
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:29,400
Yeah.

145
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,500
That's interesting. Could you give it a try?

146
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:33,700
Sure.

147
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:41,580
Over one mountain, from the direction of...
tapu-ipu-ipu, eiit!

148
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:47,160
Noo-dah!

149
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:53,500
Human to dinosaur! A dinosaur!

150
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:54,900
Yeah, yeah, I know, I know!

151
00:08:01,460 --> 00:08:02,920
W-what, what, Ch-Chief!

152
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,500
Enough! I get it, so hurry up and put it on!

153
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:10,660
Coming!

154
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:26,760
Phew, saved.

155
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:29,620
Chief! Pull yourself together! Chief!

156
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,560
I can summon a Brontosaurus, too.

157
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,720
Okay, that's enough.

158
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,480
I get it, you can use magic well enough.

159
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,900
But that's amazing.

160
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,720
Everyone who lives in Heaven can use magic.

161
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,340
Do you learn it in school classes?

162
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:44,180
I'm still far from good, though.

163
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:47,800
No, no, at that age, being able
to do that much is quite something.

164
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:50,260
Almost as good as that old man.

165
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,320
Old man?

166
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,340
Grandpa Rika?

167
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:56,360
Come to think of it, you said
"Grandpa Rika" just now...

168
00:08:56,360 --> 00:09:00,360
Could it be that the old
man's name is Rika or something?

169
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:05,220
Yes. They expected a girl to be born, so
that was the only name they had decided on.

170
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:08,280
So Grandpa's name is Hanayama Rika.

171
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,300
I'm Rika. Nice to meet you.

172
00:09:14,860 --> 00:09:17,100
It's Rika, and Rika-chan, too.

173
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,200
Hey, Ryo-san. Show me around Harajuku.

174
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:27,420
Right now? It takes almost an hour from Kameari,
you know.

175
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,500
Don't worry. I can get there in one second.

176
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:37,180
Over one mountain, hō narata,
puin puin, genchi kue, go!

177
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,840
Whoa! It vanished!

178
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:41,860
So you can teleport, too.

179
00:09:42,420 --> 00:09:45,280
Senpai, you get so many people visiting you.
That must be tough.

180
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:48,240
Hey! You're on duty, you know!

181
00:09:50,540 --> 00:09:51,900
Uncle Hanayama!

182
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:54,020
Kōme's here, you know! Kōme!

183
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,400
Where is he? Where is he hiding?!

184
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:56,740
Kōme, you hid him from me!

185
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:58,660
Where's Kōme? Where was he all along?!

186
00:09:58,660 --> 00:10:01,380
You fearsome, early good-for-nothing!

187
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:05,120
What? That man seduced
my adorable granddaughter!

188
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,440
Honestly, you're just as bad.
Why did you ever do that?

189
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:10,280
Y-yes, the real thing, my unworthy self.

190
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:13,300
Then which way is Harajuku?
Which one is Harajuku?

191
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,740
Hey, you're quick.

192
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,900
I think it's this way, I'm pretty sure.

193
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,360
No, it's not, it's this way.

194
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,500
No, I'm telling you, it's this way.

195
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:20,460
This way.

196
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:21,340
I said it's this way.

197
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:23,600
Which way was it again? Seyai!

198
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:28,120
So this goes here,
and that goes there, right?

199
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:30,600
This one's this way,
and here it goes like this, so

200
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,400
Not again.

201
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,060
It's this way.

202
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,420
Both of you are completely wrong,
aren't you?

203
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,600
Sorry.

204
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,300
It's not this way, alright?

205
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,840
Get over here right now.

206
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,500
Come back.

207
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:47,280
What?

208
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,760
Pochi-chama

209
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,540
Divine Punishment old man!

210
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:56,140
Oh my!

211
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:58,920
W-what's with that outfit?

212
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:02,400
How shameful! Change right now!

213
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:05,460
What's the big deal?
I bought it with my own money!

214
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:06,620
It's my freedom, isn't it?

215
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:10,280
What are you saying! A person from the
heavenly realm shouldn't dress like that!

216
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:13,740
Don't be so stiff!
What's wrong with a little outfit?

217
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:16,720
You should try to understand your granddaughter more,
you stubborn old man!

218
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,160
Your lecturing is too much! Just be quiet!

219
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,060
Cheers!

220
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,500
Gero gero! What am I, a frog?!

221
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,860
Ugh, I feel sick!

222
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:28,160
It's because this guy keeps getting
in the way of the conversation!

223
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,500
I'll make you throw it back up!

224
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:34,240
You bastard, how dare you pull that on me!

225
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,540
What is that, a human-faced dog?!

226
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:41,460
That's really weird!

227
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:42,920
What are you doing?!

228
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:45,900
What are you doing?!

229
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:52,180
Got it!

230
00:11:57,940 --> 00:11:59,900
Aaaaaah!

231
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:10,900
How do you like that, you bastard?! You toyed with my body however you pleased,
so I'm blowing you away!

232
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:16,700
Against the real Baisen-mai, you've got no chance.
Turning into a slug or a cockroach is the best you can expect, I'd say.

233
00:12:18,020 --> 00:12:24,900
Yeah, well, we're going to heaven together this month, right?
I'm a good kid, so I'm going home. No way!

234
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:31,360
Don't say that! Don't be so
rough with your grandchild, Rika!

235
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:37,060
You! Why do you know my name?
Of course I looked into that properly

236
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:42,500
Rika. Didn't you, in first grade, poop
in the classroom

237
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:45,680
and leave early? Noriko,

238
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:48,940
so you wet yourself, Rika.

239
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:52,600
Stop it!
Why would you tell Grandpa's secrets?

240
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:57,020
You asked, so I just answered.
Is there something wrong with that?

241
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:02,160
Well, it's not that it's bad,
it's just, my opinion, that is...

242
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:06,460
The line Rika used to win over Grandma is a masterpiece,
you know.

243
00:13:08,060 --> 00:13:10,390
Here we go. Ryo-chan,

244
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:12,480
You're here, aren't you?

245
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,840
Thanks for your hard work as always. You must have a lot to deal with too,
Ryo-chan.

246
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,340
You know, even for civil servants like me,
it's quite tough.

247
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:22,020
I have my position to consider,
so I hope you'll understand that.

248
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:26,440
Come on,
so let's just leave it at that, Ryotsu.

249
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,820
Then at least listen to
what your granddaughter says.

250
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:34,020
Just one week, until spring break ends.

251
00:13:34,020 --> 00:13:35,840
Come on,
I can stay in the lower world, can't I?

252
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:39,660
But this lower world is so filthy,
with dirty air.

253
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:41,240
And there are so many bad people.

254
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:43,700
It's not a place fit for humans to live!

255
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,340
Mind your own business!

256
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:47,940
But everyone says the lower world is fun!

257
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:51,440
I want to buy cute clothes too and
walk around Shibuya and Roppongi!

258
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,320
Don't tell such lies!
The truth is, the outer world is - !

259
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:00,620
It's a frightening place where
devils from hell come to eat humans!

260
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,180
Don't talk such nonsense!

261
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,040
That hurts, that hurts.

262
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:08,480
Raising a child with that kind of upbringing is
why she gets so fixated and runs away from home.

263
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:11,160
Dabari, dabari! If it were you, I'd
turn you into a caterpillar, you bastard!

264
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,380
Didn't she beg you in tears?

265
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:18,440
"If you won't marry me, I'll chop off my nuts and
jump into hell to kill myself," or something like that.

266
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:21,460
Konjaga banban! Konjaga banban!

267
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,840
Fine, sorry, that was an out-of-line remark.

268
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:28,500
Very well, I'll take responsibility and look after her,
so don't you worry.

269
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:32,100
But they say you should send a dear child off on a journey,
don't they?

270
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:35,100
Rest assured, we'll be looking after her,
so she'll be fine.

271
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:40,701
Hanayama-san, I understand how worried
you are about your granddaughter,

272
00:14:40,751 --> 00:14:43,480
as a grandfather myself,
I understand it well.

273
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:47,072
But think about it,
your granddaughter is already sixteen,

274
00:14:47,122 --> 00:14:51,060
and I think this is a good chance to help her grow more independent,
Hanayama-san.

275
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,220
Would that be all right?

276
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,040
Understood.

277
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,740
So it's okay, right, Grandpa?

278
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,160
Yay! Thank you, Grandpa!

279
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:07,040
But if anything happens,
you contact me right away, got it?

280
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:08,560
I'll come rushing to pick you up.

281
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,540
Yeah, got it.

282
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:14,220
And then here,
this is spending money from Grandpa.

283
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,060
Yay!

284
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:17,280
Don't tell Papa or Mama.

285
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:18,860
Thanks, Grandpa.

286
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:22,880
For a heavenly wizard,
you sure act awfully human.

287
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:27,280
Take care of yourself, Umeko.

288
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,460
Okay!

289
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,340
Bye-bye, Rika-chan!

290
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,880
Stop calling me Rika-chan!

291
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:32,860
See you.

292
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,500
Ume-chan can do anything with magic, right?

293
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,900
Yeah, pretty much.

294
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:44,140
I'll give you a soft-serve ice cream,
so come with me for a bit.

295
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:45,180
Wow, yay!

296
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:47,780
Your kindness scares me, senpai.

297
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,900
I've got a bad feeling about this.

298
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:52,020
I've got to head out for a bit now.

299
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,020
If you're going to talk, then go ahead.

300
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:54,460
Yes.

301
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:57,600
Look, Ooma-san is running
all over the place, see?

302
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:00,940
This is Mr. Ooma's sports day video,
you know.

303
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:05,140
Look at this horse called Hope of Last Place.
He's always coming in last.

304
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,360
Don't you think it's pitiful?

305
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,100
Pitiful.

306
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:11,740
Right? I'd love to make Mr. Ooma come in first,
just once.

307
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,240
Hey, Konume.

308
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:13,600
Yeah.

309
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:17,040
Then how about we make him
first with Konume's magic?

310
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:19,600
But is it really all right to do that?

311
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:23,940
Of course! If the last-place horse wins,
it's a huge long shot and a jackpot payout.

312
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:26,580
No, no, the horse will be delighted.

313
00:16:26,580 --> 00:16:30,640
Then let's go back in time together
and drop in on the sports day venue.

314
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:36,220
You fool!

315
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:37,300
Grandfather.

316
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:40,180
You still haven't gone back to heaven?

317
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:44,920
I figured as much. Just as I thought.

318
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,700
If you change the past,
the future will change.

319
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:55,740
Then I'll send you on a tour of hell.
I've seen that on a school trip, you know. Cheat or not.

320
00:16:55,740 --> 00:17:01,700
It's not some Beppu hell tour! I'm saying
I'll take you to real hell. Remember that.

321
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:09,100
Come to think of it, we learned in class that
changing the past is a violation of time law.

322
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:11,640
Then what's the point of magic, damn it!

323
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,920
Wait... so I just shouldn't change the past?

324
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,080
Konume, can you teleport to the future too?

325
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:21,780
Yes, I can.
We only just learned it last month.

326
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,980
Next Sunday. Can you go six days ahead?

327
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:26,900
I think it should be fine.

328
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:28,700
Then here I go.

329
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:33,460
One leap over the mountain,
hora, tappu-ippui!

330
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:35,880
To next Sunday, go!

331
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:48,420
Ryo-chan's group has gone awfully quiet.

332
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:50,420
I'm worried. I'll go take a look.

333
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:52,880
Senpai.

334
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,700
They're gone.

335
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,160
They vanished again.

336
00:17:57,680 --> 00:18:00,080
So she's using Konume as a taxi.

337
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:02,660
I hope they don't cause any trouble.

338
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:08,520
We did it!
We're in the future, one week later!

339
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,960
Even so,
it doesn't feel like the future at all.

340
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,960
Six days isn't enough for anything to change,
you know.

341
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,340
There I am, browsing at the bookstore.

342
00:18:20,340 --> 00:18:22,300
Here's Ryo-san's appearance six days later.

343
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:24,400
Still slacking off at work

344
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,120
Right?

345
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:27,140
Creepy.

346
00:18:27,140 --> 00:18:29,620
Reading that Edge magazine
with a goofy grin on his face,

347
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:31,880
so this is how others see us.

348
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:34,160
From now on, I'll be careful.

349
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:36,200
Look at yourself and mend your ways.

350
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,720
Konume,
go buy me the racing prediction paper.

351
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,160
Me?

352
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,920
If I go, that guy will spot me,
and we'll both be awkward.

353
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:43,800
Alright, I'm off.

354
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,140
I'll be waiting outside.

355
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:52,860
Saturday's race results should be in there.

356
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,580
Looks like we can make a killing with this.

357
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:02,260
Hurk, hurk.

358
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:02,800
Retreat!

359
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:03,800
Shee!

360
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,820
It's just a mirror.

361
00:19:05,820 --> 00:19:08,360
Turns out I'm pretty dumb

362
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:10,200
I'll go take a look.

363
00:19:11,340 --> 00:19:12,040
Senpai.

364
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:16,220
They're gone! They vanished again!

365
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,200
You're using Konume as a taxi

366
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,700
I hope they don't cause any trouble.

367
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:27,080
Senpai! Where did Konume-chan go?

368
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:28,720
Just to the future, you know.

369
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:29,660
The future?

370
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:32,640
But why the future, of all places?

371
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,120
Ta-da! I bought this.

372
00:19:35,900 --> 00:19:36,860
A racing paper?

373
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:40,660
It has the results of this Saturday's races.

374
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:43,120
You're not planning to make money off that,
are you?

375
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:47,240
Of course! In the G1 race, a super
long-shot payout is coming up for Senpai!

376
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,520
Even if we bet 10,000 yen,
we'd get 10 million.

377
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:52,520
If we bet 1 million yen,
we'd get a whopping 1 billion yen!

378
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:56,100
But where would the money to bet come from?

379
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:59,760
Exactly, Senpai. You lost big at pachinko,
so you shouldn't even have a thousand yen.

380
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:02,720
That's why, Gaga-kun,
lend me about a million yen, won't you?

381
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:04,120
Kei-chan, don't lend it to him!

382
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:05,980
I know, I won't.

383
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:09,600
The Chief has also forbidden
us from lending Senpai money.

384
00:20:10,660 --> 00:20:17,960
Don't say that. If I win, I'll pay you back double. Well, ten times...
no, I'll add 100 million yen in interest, so come on!

385
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:21,040
What a profitable business proposal,
isn't it?

386
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:34,100
Boo-boo, did you perhaps hear everything just now?
No, it was all a joke, a joke, of course it was a joke, you didn't think I was serious, did you?

387
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,540
Please don't mind it.

388
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:36,420
Chief...

389
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:37,220
Idiot!

390
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:40,540
What is this guy thinking,
being a police officer?

391
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:42,100
I told you, it was a joke.

392
00:20:42,100 --> 00:20:44,500
You're still saying that?

393
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,080
Turn your back for a second
and you're at it again.

394
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,680
It was only an attempt,
so please forgive him.

395
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,300
Konume, you understand, right?

396
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:53,480
You shouldn't get involved
with Ryo-chan anymore.

397
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:56,840
Tei-chan and I will take you to Harajuku or Roppongi,
wherever you want.

398
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:57,400
Really?

399
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,640
Let's go out for a meal,
just the three of us.

400
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,320
Yay!

401
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:04,060
Hey! You lot,
don't you dare sweet-talk Konume!

402
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:05,740
That girl relies on me!

403
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:09,560
Too bad, from now on we'll
be looking after Konume-chan.

404
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,620
Ryo-chan, be my guest.

405
00:21:11,620 --> 00:21:15,160
Damn it, at this rate that
super long-shot jackpot will...

406
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:18,960
Alright, alright, Chief, I was wrong.

407
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:20,780
What a lie!

408
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,800
Hey! With just this, we can...!

409
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:23,460
Here it comes!

410
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,920
Hey! What do you think you're doing?

411
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:32,420
We crossed one mountain and then...

412
00:21:32,420 --> 00:21:33,180
Hop, hop!

413
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:35,560
Go to ten a.m. yesterday!

414
00:21:37,460 --> 00:21:38,780
They vanished!

415
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,020
What do we do?

416
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:42,040
Konume, can't you call Grandpa?

417
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:42,480
I see.

418
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:46,500
Grandpa, it's terrible! Come quickly!

419
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:50,820
Yay!

420
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:53,660
What's wrong, Konume?

421
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,040
Grandpa...

422
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:59,300
Well, I was busy helping with
the rest of your vacation.

423
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:03,960
It's terrible, Grandpa. Actually...

424
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:08,800
What? I told him not to go back to the past,
that big idiot!

425
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:11,360
Didn't he say he was
going to yesterday at ten?

426
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:15,380
I get it. Ten o'clock is when
the pachinko parlors open!

427
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:20,320
I see. Senpai plans to put the money he was
going to lose at pachinko into the horse races!

428
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:22,340
Alright, let's go after them right away!

429
00:22:28,940 --> 00:22:30,660
What are you lot doing?

430
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:33,040
Hey, Ryo-san, Ryo-san, didn't he come by?

431
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:34,880
Who are you?

432
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:36,260
It's Konume, silly.

433
00:22:36,260 --> 00:22:39,760
Konume, since you ran away from home,
that means it's tomorrow for you.

434
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:42,240
Ryo-chan can't tell that at this point.

435
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:43,020
I see.

436
00:22:43,020 --> 00:22:45,880
Hey, Ryo,
didn't you come here from tomorrow?

437
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:48,000
What are you babbling about?

438
00:22:48,580 --> 00:22:49,480
Sorry to keep you waiting.

439
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:50,640
Got back from the shopping run.

440
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:52,320
Today we're going to make a killing!

441
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:56,260
Judging by the look of things,
Senpai hasn't come here.

442
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:57,720
What's wrong?

443
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:58,900
Right.

444
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,740
We've gone to a different era.

445
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:33,160
A castle? It's Nikko Edo Village, is it?

446
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:35,260
No, maybe it's the Kyoto Movie Village.

447
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:38,740
We were in such a rush that we
must have messed up the magic spell.

448
00:23:39,460 --> 00:23:42,120
Hey, what nonsense are you babbling about?

449
00:23:42,120 --> 00:23:44,560
Don't get so worked up about it.
You're a part-timer, aren't you?

450
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:46,140
You suspicious fellow.

451
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:49,680
That looks like a real sword!
Let me borrow it for a sec.

452
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:50,460
Be quiet!

453
00:23:56,740 --> 00:23:57,460
The real deal!

454
00:23:58,400 --> 00:23:59,140
Yay!

455
00:23:59,620 --> 00:24:00,940
What's going on?!

456
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:03,500
Assemble! Assemble!

457
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:04,980
A suspicious intruder has sneaked in!

458
00:24:05,300 --> 00:24:06,100
Intruder!

459
00:24:06,540 --> 00:24:09,140
Haven't you found the intruder yet?

460
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:12,000
Catch them before they get far away!

461
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:16,840
Looks like we've come
to a crazy time period.

462
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:19,380
Anyway, we can't stay like this.

463
00:24:19,380 --> 00:24:21,800
Should we dress up so no one gets
suspicious and check things out?

464
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:24,680
One mountain down

465
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:25,480
Coming, coming!

466
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:27,060
Change into samurai clothes!

467
00:24:28,340 --> 00:24:31,020
What's this "gero gero" thing?!

468
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:33,080
Right, I'm getting the incantation wrong.

469
00:24:33,220 --> 00:24:35,860
Hondaratta, poi poi.

470
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:38,300
Wh-wh-wait, that's wrong!

471
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:40,500
Hondaratta, hoh hoh.

472
00:24:41,040 --> 00:24:41,920
Hoh hoh.

473
00:24:41,940 --> 00:24:43,540
Whoa, I got it wrong again.

474
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:45,900
What was it again?

475
00:24:46,360 --> 00:24:46,720
That's it!

476
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,960
Hondaratta, pui pui!

477
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:54,280
This way, no one will suspect us.

478
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:55,560
Oi, monkey!

479
00:24:55,900 --> 00:24:58,120
Monkey? Where's a monkey?

480
00:24:58,120 --> 00:24:59,480
Don't play dumb, monkey.

481
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,780
I'm talking about you, aren't I?

482
00:25:00,780 --> 00:25:01,280
Me?

483
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:02,620
What are you doing here?

484
00:25:02,620 --> 00:25:03,940
Uh, no...

485
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:07,980
I was just checking the shrubbery for
any suspicious characters hiding in it.

486
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:08,360
I see.

487
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:09,380
Never mind that, monkey!

488
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:11,860
Lord Nobunaga should be waking up soon.

489
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,380
Lord Nobunaga?

490
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:16,480
We're fine here, so go back to Zōri-tori.

491
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:21,940
Nobunaga? I've heard that name somewhere.

492
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:25,480
Oh no, I'm bad at history.

493
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:30,840
Hey, faster!

494
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:34,240
Yes! This is how you accelerate!
Watch closely!

495
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:39,720
What a run, it vanished in an instant.

496
00:25:45,120 --> 00:25:46,940
Honda-kun, you came. Thanks.

497
00:25:47,460 --> 00:25:49,760
Senpai, what happened to your outfit?

498
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:52,160
It's a long story,
so I'll give you the short version.

499
00:25:53,080 --> 00:25:54,140
Lord Nobunaga.

500
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:55,560
That's right.

501
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:58,800
We're in the era where
Nobunaga is alive right now.

502
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:00,880
Come on, senpai.

503
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,580
Trying to pull my leg won't work.

504
00:26:02,580 --> 00:26:04,040
I'm not lying. Look.

505
00:26:05,340 --> 00:26:06,920
Isn't that a castle?

506
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:10,000
Is this Nikko Edo Village,
or the Edo Village in Kyoto?

507
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,840
Don't react the same way I did.

508
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:14,480
Anyway, in that getup,
you'll definitely blend right in.

509
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:19,220
Cross one mountain, then tapui-pui,
and still become a samurai!

510
00:26:22,980 --> 00:26:23,920
Aaaaaaah!

511
00:26:24,080 --> 00:26:24,940
There, that should do.

512
00:26:24,940 --> 00:26:29,720
W-wow, senpai, you look like a wizard!
What happened?

513
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,620
It would take a long time to explain.

514
00:26:31,620 --> 00:26:34,440
Could this be a dream I'm having?

515
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:34,600
A dream?

516
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:41,120
Wait. Maybe it's more convenient to
let him keep thinking it's a dream.

517
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:45,560
That's right, this is inside your dream.

518
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:50,340
Then why didn't you say so first?
I thought something was off!

519
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:53,740
By the way, you were a big fan
of period dramas on TV, right?

520
00:26:55,020 --> 00:26:57,460
Leave period dramas to me!

521
00:26:57,460 --> 00:26:58,760
People call me...

522
00:27:00,380 --> 00:27:02,700
They call him the period drama doctor.

523
00:27:03,540 --> 00:27:04,460
Just the characters "da" and "no"?

524
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:08,180
So who's this Honda Nobunaga?

525
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:11,840
Oda Nobunaga was a Sengoku-era warlord, you know.
Isn't he famous?

526
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:14,260
He's the guy who tried to unify the country.

527
00:27:15,140 --> 00:27:18,720
But it was actually Toyotomi Hideyoshi
who unified the country, though.

528
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,400
I've heard that guy's name before.

529
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:21,060
Yeah.

530
00:27:23,620 --> 00:27:24,820
Someone's there.

531
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:28,100
A weirdo shows up and
everyone's freaking out over it,

532
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:30,640
but there's always one
like that in every era

533
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,760
That's right. Well, since it's a dream,
it's an interesting development, isn't it.

534
00:28:10,900 --> 00:28:14,740
Speaking of which, that samurai we met
earlier called me a monkey or something.

535
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:18,740
He probably mistook you for this guy.
"Monkey" was Hideyoshi's nickname.

536
00:28:18,980 --> 00:28:21,600
But a gorilla fits better than a monkey,
doesn't it?

537
00:28:21,920 --> 00:28:22,840
Don't say unnecessary things!

538
00:28:23,060 --> 00:28:26,720
Excuse me, what are you two
going on about that makes no sense?

539
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:30,240
For a man who's going to conquer the land,
you look awfully unreliable.

540
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:30,880
Yeah, right.

541
00:28:31,400 --> 00:28:33,020
Are you seriously going to put out the fire?

542
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:33,660
Yes.

543
00:28:33,660 --> 00:28:34,240
Eh…

544
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,000
Mm…

545
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,800
Why don't you dig somewhere too, Kyō-chan?

546
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:41,720
You might find hidden treasure from the Tokugawa or Toyotomi clans,
you know?

547
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:43,760
Mm…

548
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:44,440
Whoa!

549
00:28:44,680 --> 00:28:48,020
Honda! Does Hideyoshi have piles
of oban and koban gold coins?

550
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:52,360
Well, he took control of the realm and became kampaku,
so he must have been incredibly rich.

551
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:54,900
I see, incredibly rich.

552
00:28:54,900 --> 00:28:55,980
Phew…

553
00:28:56,600 --> 00:29:00,660
This might be better than
making money at the horse races.

554
00:29:00,660 --> 00:29:03,000
Nyehehehehe

